    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "FKconvergence: unpublished Lean 4 development by Zijie Zhuang (2026), not publicly accessible",
        "note": "An earlier Lean 4 development by the same author on the critical planar FK (random-cluster) model on the square lattice with 1 <= q < 4. It has not been published and is not publicly accessible; there is no URL, release or commit that could be cited, so it is identified by its project name, FKconvergence. 172 of the 873 modules under PottsDiscontinuity/ (about 24,000 of 120,000 lines) are adapted from it, and each of them says so in its header: 57 in FK/ (finite FK measures on graphs, boundary conditions, positive association, comparison and finite-energy inequalities, box limits), 42 in Duality/ (planar duality) and 73 in TorusTopology/ and TorusExploration/ (discrete topology of the lattice and its medial graph). The extent of adaptation ranges from relocating namespaces and imports only (about 60 modules) to generalizing the parameters to independent 0 < p < 1 and q >= 1 with no upper bound on q (about 50 modules) and connecting the code to this development's FK library (about 40 modules); a few modules adapt individual arguments, for example comparison inequalities reversed for wired boundary conditions. The statements of the three main theorems and their 17 definitions (PottsDiscontinuity/Frozen/) were transcribed from the paper and are not taken from it; the other modules under PottsDiscontinuity/ were written for this development.",
        "relationship": "adapts"
      }
